         recommended test: After the change, the tool still identifies at least the same defects it identified before.
           inputs:  Use a two-run or two-stage fixture where enumeration returns defects for an obligation id that is not present in the current mapped-evidence batch, and where verdict returns only a subset of the enumerated defects. Also include a case where the response model types are the new `_Enumeration` / `_DefectVerdicts` types, so the test can detect if the pipeline drops previously collected `ObligationDiscrimination` items or skips unmapped-but-enumerated defects.
